From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 12:17:34 +0200
Subject: leds: lgm-sso: fill in the rate of the unprogrammed blink rank

sso_init_freq() stores 0 for rank 0 and delay_to_freq_idx() divides by
it. A blink_set with both delays zero -- what the timer trigger passes
on a fresh activation, and what the LED core documents as "pick a
sensible default" -- computes (1000 / priv->freq[0]) / 2. MIPS builds
pass -mno-check-zero-division, so it does not trap: both delays come
back as 4294967295, the software blink timer is armed some 49 days out
and the lamp latches in whichever phase it happened to be in. An
architecture that does trap gets a division-by-zero oops in blink_set
instead.

Rank 0 is not a rate of its own. sso_led_freq_set() returns early for
it, leaving the pin's blink registers as found, and a zero in those
registers is -- in the same encoding that function writes for the ranks
it does program, source select 0 for FPID and rate 0 for freq_div_tbl[0]
-- the rate of rank 1. On the 8 kHz FPID clock these SoCs carry, that is
2 Hz, and 2 Hz is what a pin whose blink registers have never been
written blinks at.

Store that rate instead of zero. The both-zero default becomes 250 ms on
and 250 ms off, which is what the pin will do, and desc->blink_rate
stops reading 0 for an LED with no intel,sso-blink-rate-hz.

A requested rate of 2 Hz or less now selects rank 0 rather than rank 1,
so it is served by the blink registers as found instead of being written
there. Both are the same rate.

No device tree in tree sets intel,sso-hw-blink, without which
delay_to_freq_idx() is never reached.

Fixes: c3987cd2bca3 ("leds: lgm: Add LED controller driver for LGM SoC")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c b/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c
index ede959c4dc94..dda4e4fa7980 100644
--- a/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c
@@ -440,7 +440,13 @@ static void sso_init_freq(struct sso_led_priv *priv)
 {
 	int i;
 
-	priv->freq[0] = 0;
+	/*
+	 * Rank 0 is not a rate of its own: sso_led_freq_set() skips it and the
+	 * pin keeps whatever its blink registers hold. Those are zero at
+	 * reset, which in the encoding the function writes for every other
+	 * rank is the FPID source at freq_div_tbl[0] -- the rate of rank 1.
+	 */
+	priv->freq[0] = priv->fpid_clkrate / freq_div_tbl[0];
 	for (i = 1; i < MAX_FREQ_RANK; i++) {
 		if (i < MAX_FPID_FREQ_RANK) {
 			priv->freq[i] = priv->fpid_clkrate / freq_div_tbl[i - 1];
